--TEST--
An `IOError` wrapping a cause carries it at `previous` with the cause's own location and message untouched, and the chain walks to a `null` end — `rule:errors/propagation` and `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: IOError
// The everyday shape for this class: a helper that knows what it was doing
// wraps the failure that knows what went wrong. Asked as a walk to the end of
// the chain rather than one `previous` read, so a wrap that kept only the
// nearest cause fails here while printing a plausible first line.
class Wrap {
    public static function three(): void {
        try {
            try {
                throw new ParseError("the document is not a document");
            } catch (ParseError $inner) {
                throw new IOError("the saved report is unusable", {previous: $inner});
            }
        } catch (IOError $middle) {
            throw new IOError("the nightly run has nothing to send", {previous: $middle});
        }
    }
}

try {
    Wrap::three();
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (IOError $outer) {
    echo $outer->message, "\n";
    uint $depth = 0;
    var $cursor = $outer->previous;
    while ($cursor != null) {
        $depth = $depth + 1;
        echo "  ", $depth, ": ", $cursor->message, "\n";
        // `?->` and not `->`: assigning to the binding being narrowed drops the
        // narrowing for the right-hand side of that very statement.
        $cursor = $cursor?->previous;
    }
    // Three errors, so two causes and then the end of the chain. Counted,
    // because a walk that stopped at the first cause prints a plausible line
    // and a wrong number.
    echo "causes=", $depth, "\n";
}

// Wrapping is not rethrowing: the cause keeps the place it was raised at, and
// the wrapper's own location is the line that wrapped it. Compared rather than
// printed, because a case's file name is not part of what this pins.
try {
    try {
        throw new ParseError("bad field");
    } catch (ParseError $cause) {
        throw new IOError("could not read it", {previous: $cause});
    }
} catch (IOError $wrapper) {
    var $kept = $wrapper->previous;
    if ($kept != null) {
        if ($kept->location != $wrapper->location) {
            echo "the cause kept its own place\n";
        }
        if ($kept->message == "bad field") {
            echo "and its own message\n";
        }
    }
}

// An error raised on its own has no cause at all, which is what makes the walk
// above terminate rather than loop.
try {
    throw new IOError("nothing underneath");
} catch (IOError $alone) {
    if ($alone->previous == null) {
        echo "no cause\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
the nightly run has nothing to send
  1: the saved report is unusable
  2: the document is not a document
causes=2
the cause kept its own place
and its own message
no cause
